  "id": "gilles-de-la-tourettes-syndrome",
  "term": "Gilles de la Tourette’s syndrome",
  "definition": "Gilles de la Tourette’s syndrome is a neuropsychological disorder involving changes in dopamine-related brain signaling within frontal-subcortical circuits. It is marked by multiple motor tics and at least one vocal tic occurring many times a day on most days for more than a year, beginning before age 18, and causing significant distress or impairment.",
